      "question": {
        ":question/id": "a4a4f60b-f7bb-5734-8d87-39b4cdc62f9e",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Consider a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =2 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+0 & =2 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
